(d) A farmer's market where persons offer the sale of agricultural products including value-added agricultural products and; or
(e) A county sponsored event.
(Ord. No. 2014-12, § 1, 8-28-2014)

438:
(a) All applications for licenses for flea markets shall be submitted to code enforcement on a form prescribed by code enforcement. Said application shall include, but not be limited to, the following:
(1) Name and address of the applicant; if the applicant is a partnership, the names and addresses of the partners; if the applicant is a corporation, the names and addresses of the officers and directors;
(2) Name and address of the owner of the land upon which the flea market is to be located. In the event that the applicant intends to locate and/or operate a flea market on leased property, a copy of the lease shall be submitted with the application. If, however, the property is owned by the applicant, said applicant shall attach to the application a copy of the deed conveying title unto the applicant;
(3) Telephone number of the applicant;
(4) The affidavit of each person whose name appears on an application for a license pursuant to subsection swearing that such person has not been convicted of or entered a plea of nolo contendere to any felony within five years prior to the date of the application or been convicted of or entered a plea of nolo contender to any misdemeanor involving crimes of moral turpitude, gambling, sexual offenses, assault, battery, any violation of the "Family Violence Act", or illegal drugs.
(5) Date of birth and identification (i.e., driver's license) of the applicant;
(6) Fingerprints of applicant;
(b) All applications for a license to operate a booth within a flea market shall be submitted to code enforcement on a form prescribed by code enforcement. Said application shall include, but not be limited to, the following:
(1) Name and address of the applicant; if the applicant is a partnership, the names and addresses of the partners; if the applicant is a corporation, the names and addresses of the officers and directors;
(2) Name and address of the flea market within which the booth will be located;
(3) Telephone number of the applicant;
(4) The affidavit of each person whose name appears on an application for a license pursuant to subsection swearing that such person has not been convicted of or entered a plea of nolo contendere to any felony within five years prior to the date of the application or been convicted of or entered a plea of nolo contender to any misdemeanor involving crimes of moral turpitude, gambling, sexual offenses, assault, battery, any violation of the "Family Violence Act", or illegal drugs.
(5) Date of birth and identification (i.e., driver's license) of the applicant; and
(6) Fingerprints of applicant.
(Ord. No. 2014-12, § 1, 8-28-2014)

486:
No person shall cause, suffer or allow open burning in any area of the county without a permit except as follows:
(1) For the recreational purpose of cooking food for immediate human consumption;
(2) Fires set for the purpose of training firefighting personnel authorized by the county director of fire and emergency services;
(3) Operation of devices using open flames such as tar kettles, blow torches, welding torches, portable heaters, and other flame-making equipment where approved safety measures are used;
(4) Setting and maintenance by contractors and tradesmen of miscellaneous small warming fires for their workers.
(Code 1992, § 9-49; Ord. No. 97-11, 10-23-1997)
